              "type": "text",
              "text": "<h3><strong><strong>About This Masterclass</strong></strong><br></h3><p>Ansel Adams famously noted: <em><em>“You don't take a photograph, you make it.”</em></em></p><p>At its heart, photography isn't about stealing a fleeting moment from time, it’s about deliberately constructing a visual story.</p><p>I’m <strong><strong>Sarmad Hasan</strong></strong>, a professional photographer and documentary filmmaker with over 15 years behind the lens. Throughout my career, I’ve created visual content for global organizations and brands including <strong><strong>Coca-Cola, the UN, the British Council, and TEDx</strong></strong>. I’m running this walking masterclass to pass on real-world visual grammar, deliberate framing techniques, and spatial discipline to dedicated photographers ready to elevate their craft.</p><p>Moving from the brutalist geometry of the <strong><strong>Barbican Estate</strong></strong>, down through historic City passages, across the river, and culminating along the kinetic backdrops of the <strong><strong>South Bank</strong></strong>, we will spend three hours putting advanced visual storytelling and narrative exposure techniques into practice.</p><p><strong><strong>Your ticket includes:</strong></strong></p><ul><li><strong><strong>3 hours of intensive, on-street mentoring</strong></strong> covering advanced composition and narrative shutter/exposure techniques with live, real-time feedback.</li><li><strong><strong>Strict 6-person cohort cap</strong></strong> to ensure uncompromised, 1-on-1 guidance throughout the route.</li><li><strong><strong>5 professionally retouched portraits of yourself</strong></strong> taken by me during the walk and delivered in high resolution post-workshop.</li></ul>",
