          "widgets": {
            "faqs": [
              {
                "question": "What skill level is required?",
                "answer": "This workshop is geared towards intermediate and advanced photographers. You should already have a solid understanding of manual exposure (aperture, shutter speed, ISO) and how your specific camera functions, as the focus will be entirely on creative direction, framing, and light."
              },
              {
                "question": "What gear do I need to bring? ",
                "answer": "An interchangeable-lens camera (mirrorless or DSLR) is required for this masterclass. Prime lenses (35mm, 50mm, or 85mm) or a fast standard zoom (such as a 24–70mm f/2.8) are strongly recommended. Variable ND filters would be a huge plus."
              },
              {
                "question": "How do the included portraits of me work?",
                "answer": "During key portrait setups across the route, I illustrate some of these techniques with you as the subject. You will receive 5 high-resolution, professionally retouched portraits delivered via a private digital download link within 3-5 business days following the workshop."
              },
              {
                "question": "Where exactly are we meeting?",
                "answer": "We will meet directly outdoors at the Lakeside Terrace, right by the water basin in front of St Giles Cripplegate (accessible via the main Barbican Centre ground level or descending from the highwalks)."
              },
              {
                "question": "What happens if it rains?",
                "answer": "The masterclass goes ahead in light rain—wet urban pavements, reflections, and moodier light create fantastic storytelling elements. Significant portions of the Barbican also feature covered highwalks. In the event of severe weather, the session will be rescheduled."
              },
              {
                "question": "What is the refund policy?",
                "answer": "Tickets are refundable upto two weeks before the session date. However, life happens—if for any reason you are unable to make it to this session, you won’t lose your spot. You will be able to roll your ticket over and attend the next scheduled masterclass at no additional cost."
              }
            ],
